# Stray text after a field is blamed, not the field it cut short (`0` is not checked as a day).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | extend x = datetime(2024-01-0é)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..42
  PIPELINE@0..41
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    EXTEND_OP@9..41
      IDENT@9..15 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@16..41
        NAME@16..17
          IDENT@16..17 "x"
        WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
        EQ@18..19 "="
        WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
        LITERAL@20..41
          DATETIME@20..41 "datetime(2024-01-0é)"
  WHITESPACE@41..42 "\n"

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2024-01-0é`
  --> query:1:39
  |
1 | from t | extend x = datetime(2024-01-0é)
  |                                       ^ unexpected text after the date
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`
